<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="MAL" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Malachi</para>
  <para style="mt">Malachi</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The burden of the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> by Mal’akh <char style="add">[My messenger]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />I have loved you, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. Yet you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, Wherein have you<char style="ord">i</char> loved us? <char style="add">[Was]</char> not ‘Esav <char style="add">[Hairy]</char> Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>’s brother? says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: yet I loved Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And I hated ‘Esav <char style="add">[Hairy]</char>, and laid his mountains and his heritage waste for the dragons of the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Whereas Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> says, We are impoverished, but we will return and build the desolate places; thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, They shall build, but I will throw down; and they shall call them, The border of wickedness, and, The people against whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has indignation forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And your eyes shall see, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall say, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will be magnified from the border of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />A son honors <char style="add">[his]</char> father, and a servant his master: if then I <char style="add">[be]</char> a father, where <char style="add">[is]</char> my honour? and if I <char style="add">[be]</char> a master, where <char style="add">[is]</char> my fear? says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> unto you, O priests, that despise my name. And you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, Wherein have we despised you<char style="ord">i</char> name?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> offer polluted bread upon my altar; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, Wherein have we polluted you<char style="ord">i</char>? In that you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, The table of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> contemptible.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And if you<char style="ord">2f</char> offer the blind for sacrifice, <char style="add">[is it]</char> not evil? and if you<char style="ord">2f</char> offer the lame and sick, <char style="add">[is it]</char> not evil? offer it now unto you<char style="ord">i</char> governor; will he be pleased with you<char style="ord">i</char>, or accept you<char style="ord">i</char> person? says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And now, I pray you, beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> that he will be gracious unto us: this has been by your means: will he regard your persons? says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Who <char style="add">[is there]</char> even among you that would shut the doors <char style="add">[for nothing]</char>? neither do you<char style="ord">2f</char> kindle <char style="add">[fire]</char> on my altar for nothing. I have no pleasure in you, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, neither will I accept an offering at your hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For from the rising of the sun even unto the going down of the same my name <char style="add">[shall be]</char> great among the Gentiles; and in every place incense <char style="add">[shall be]</char> offered unto my name, and a pure offering: for my name <char style="add">[shall be]</char> great among the heathen, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />But you<char style="ord">2f</char> have profaned it, in that you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, The table of the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All] [is]</char> polluted; and the fruit thereof, <char style="add">[even]</char> his meat, <char style="add">[is]</char> contemptible.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> said also, Behold, what a weariness <char style="add">[is it]</char>! and you<char style="ord">2f</char> have snuffed at it, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> brought <char style="add">[that which was]</char> torn, and the lame, and the sick; thus you<char style="ord">2f</char> brought an offering: should I accept this of your hand? says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But cursed <char style="add">[be]</char> the deceiver, which has in his flock a male, and vows, and sacrifices unto the Lord a corrupt thing: for I <char style="add">[am]</char> a great King, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, and my name <char style="add">[is]</char> dreadful among the heathen.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And now, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> priests, this commandment <char style="add">[is]</char> for you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">2f</char> will not hear, and if you<char style="ord">2f</char> will not lay <char style="add">[it]</char> to heart, to give glory unto my name, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, I will even send a curse upon you, and I will curse your blessings: yes, I have cursed them already, because you<char style="ord">2f</char> do not lay <char style="add">[it]</char> to heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Behold, I will corrupt your seed, and spread dung upon your faces, <char style="add">[even]</char> the dung of your solemn feasts; and <char style="add">[one]</char> shall take you away with it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I have sent this commandment unto you, that my covenant might be with Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />My covenant was with him of life and peace; and I gave them to him <char style="add">[for]</char> the fear which he feared me, and was afraid before my name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />The law of twas in his mouth, and iniquity was not found in his lips: he walked with me in peace and equity, and did turn many away from iniquity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For the priest’s lips should keep knowledge, and they should seek the Torah at his mouth: for he <char style="add">[is]</char> the messenger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But you<char style="ord">2f</char> are departed out of the way; you<char style="ord">2f</char> have caused many to stumble at the law; you<char style="ord">2f</char> have corrupted the covenant of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Therefore have I also made you contemptible and base before all the people, according as you<char style="ord">2f</char> have not kept my ways, but have been partial in the law.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Have we not all one father? has not one God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> created us? why do we deal treacherously every man against his brother, by profaning the covenant of our fathers?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> has dealt treacherously, and an abomination is committed in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; for Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> has profaned the holiness of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> which he loved, and has married the daughter of a strange god.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will cut off the man that does this, the master and the scholar, out of the tabernacles of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, and him that offers an offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And this have you<char style="ord">2f</char> done again, covering the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with tears, with weeping, and with crying out, insomuch that he regards not the offering any more, or receives <char style="add">[it]</char> with good will at your hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Yet you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, For what reason? Because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has been witness between you<char style="ord">i</char> and the wife of you<char style="ord">i</char> youth, against whom you<char style="ord">i</char> have dealt treacherously: yet <char style="add">[is]</char> she you<char style="ord">i</char> companion, and the wife of you<char style="ord">i</char> covenant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And did not he make one? Yet had he the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of the spirit. And wherefore one? That he might seek a godly seed. Therefore take heed to your spirit, and let none deal treacherously against the wife of his youth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />For the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, says that he hates putting away: for <char style="add">[one]</char> covers violence with his garment, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>: therefore take heed to your spirit, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> deal not treacherously.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> have wearied the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with your words. Yet you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, Wherein have we wearied <char style="add">[him]</char>? When you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, Every one that does evil <char style="add">[is]</char> good in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and he delights in them; or, Where <char style="add">[is]</char> the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of judgment?</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Behold, I will send my messenger, and he shall prepare the way before me: and the Lord-Adon <char style="add">[Ruler of the Earth]</char>, whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> seek, shall suddenly come to his temple, even the messenger of the covenant, whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> delight in: behold, he shall come, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />But who may abide the day of his coming? and who shall stand when he appears? for he <char style="add">[is]</char> like a refiner’s fire, and like fullers’ soap:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he shall sit <char style="add">[as]</char> a refiner and purifier of silver: and he shall purify the sons of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char>, and purge them as gold and silver, that they may offer unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> an offering in righteousness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then shall the offering of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> be pleasant unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as in the days of old, and as in former years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And I will come near to you to judgment; and I will be a swift witness against the sorcerers, and against the adulterers, and against false swearers, and against those that oppress the employee <char style="pn">(hired laborer)</char> in <char style="add">[his]</char> wages, the widow, and the fatherless, and that turn aside the stranger <char style="add">[from his right]</char>, and fear not me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, I change not; therefore you<char style="ord">2f</char> sons of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char> are not consumed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Even from the days of your fathers you<char style="ord">2f</char> are gone away from my ordinances, and have not kept <char style="add">[them]</char>. Return unto me, and I will return unto you, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>. But you<char style="ord">2f</char> said, Wherein shall we return?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Will a man rob God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>? Yet you<char style="ord">2f</char> have robbed me. But you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, Wherein have we robbed you<char style="ord">i</char>? In tithes and offerings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> cursed with a curse: for you<char style="ord">2f</char> have robbed me, <char style="add">[even]</char> this whole nation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Bring you<char style="ord">2f</char> all the tithes into the storehouse, that there may be meat in my house, and prove me now with this, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, if I will not open you the windows of heaven, and pour you out a blessing, that <char style="add">[there shall]</char> not <char style="add">[be room]</char> enough <char style="add">[to receive it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And I will rebuke <char style="pn">(reprimand; strongly warn; restrain)</char> the devourer for your sakes, and he shall not destroy the fruits of your ground; neither shall your vine cast her fruit before the time in the field, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And all nations shall call you Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char>: for you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be a delightsome land, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Your words have been stout against me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. Yet you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, What have we spoken <char style="add">[so much]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> have said, It <char style="add">[is]</char> vain to serve God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and what profit <char style="add">[is it]</char> that we have kept his ordinance, and that we have walked mournfully before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And now we call the proud happy; yes, they that work wickedness are set up; yes, <char style="add">[they that]</char> tempt God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> are even delivered.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then they that feared the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke often one to another: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> listened, and heard <char style="add">[it]</char>, and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and that thought upon his name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they shall be my, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, in that day when I make up my jewels; and I will spare them, as a man spares his own son that serves him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> return, and discern between the righteous and the wicked, between him that serves God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> and him that serves him not.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />For, behold, the day comes, that shall burn as an oven; and all the proud, yes, and all that do wickedly, shall be stubble: and the day that comes shall burn them up, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, that it shall leave them neither root nor branch.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall trample down the wicked; for they shall be ashes under the soles of your feet in the day that I shall do <char style="add">[this]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Remember you<char style="ord">2f</char> the law of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horev <char style="add">[Desert]</char> for all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[with]</char> the statutes and judgments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Behold, I will send you Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> the prophet before the coming of the great and dreadful day of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he shall turn the heart of the fathers to the children, and the heart of the children to their fathers, lest I come and strike the earth with utter destruction.</para>
</usx>